-- title:
--   Adding a constant on the right leaves the gradient unchanged
-- statement:
--   Let $g : E \to \mathbb{R}$ be differentiable on a real inner product space $E$, and let $c \in \mathbb{R}$. Adding the constant $c$ on the right does not change the gradient: for every $z \in E$,
--   $$\nabla (w \mapsto g(w) + c)(z) = \nabla g(z).$$
--   Here $\nabla$ denotes the gradient, i.e. the Riesz representative of the Fréchet derivative, and the identity holds in $E$.
-- source:
